          "source_quote": "ὑπὸ τῆς συνοίας ἐξώκειλα εἰς νόσον",
          "english_quote": "Through brooding I drifted into illness.",
          "issue": "The draft preserves a nautical association but substitutes drifting for the running-aground image of ἐξώκειλα. The note mentions running aground without preserving that image in the main text.",
          "suggested_revision": "Compare and adopt a source-transparent rendering such as “Through brooding I ran aground in illness,” updating the lexical note accordingly. The revised wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ αὐτὸν Σίμωνα νῦν οὐ διὰ φιλομάθειαν αὐτὸν εἰς φιλίαν προσέμενον",
          "english_quote": "and that even now he welcomed Simon into friendship not from love of learning",
          "issue": "The emphasis associated with αὐτὸν Σίμωνα has been transferred to νῦν. “Even now” introduces temporal emphasis, whereas the source foregrounds Simon himself.",
          "suggested_revision": "Render “and that he now welcomed even Simon himself into friendship, not from love of learning.” Preserve the following explanation of Apion's motive.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
